        "_uid": "6610f514-90d7-dd49-26c1-382ee542e548",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Dr Jafri added,\"In the past 20 to 30 years, Hepatitis C produce chronically in more than 70 percent- 90 percent of the cases and chronic liver disease (Cirrhosis) develops in 20 percent-30 percent of patients. Bad hygiene, infected water and food transmit types A and E whereas types B, C, and 0 are mainly through blood, blood products and sexual contacts. The source of infection is unknown in one third of Hepatitis B and one half of Hepatitis C.\" ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Dr Jafri concluded by saying that Hepatitis Band C could result in chronic Liver disease and Liver Cancer. Active and passive prophylaxis is available for Hepatitis A and B only.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
