    "show_share": true,
    "description": "\"Diagnosis of acute viral Hepatitis is established by blood tests and are presented in two modes, i.e. Jaundice and Non-Jaundice. Out of five serologically distinguishable types - Hepatitis B, C and 0 may culminates in chronic types\", informed Dr Wasim Jafri, Consultant Gastroentrologist and Associate Professor of Medicine, The Aga Khan University Hospital, Karachi. He was giving a presentation on \"Hepatitis A to E and Liver Cancer\" at 'Signs, Symptoms and Care', monthly health awareness program, held on December 18, 1999.",
